{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T20:18:59.522Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"df02aa70db5bf450de2ff7ae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-zi34i1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A nested SDK dispatch for another tracker reuses the caller's active extension scope, so the second tracker's guards and extension fields never load"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported by the Codex review of PR 1764. The active extension scope is one process-local boolean (activeExtensionScope in src/sdk/runtime.ts). runAction, PmClient item-transaction helpers and runInActiveExtensionScope all skip activation when it is set, without comparing the tracker the scope was opened for. A host that opens runWithActiveExtensions for tracker A and then dispatches a mutation for tracker B inside the callback runs it under A's registrations: a beforeMutation guard installed only in B never judges the write, and B's extension fields are unknown. The same call made outside the scope activates B and is refused. The behaviour predates PR 1764; the new finalize step inherits it through the shared rule."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","extensions","guards","multi-tracker"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-21T20:18:59.522Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T20:18:59.522Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The active extension scope records the resolved tracker root it was opened for; A dispatch or runInActiveExtensionScope call for a different root activates that root's extensions or refuses with a typed error naming both roots, never reusing the other tracker's registrations; A spec installs a refusing guard in tracker B only and proves the nested write is judged; Same-root nesting keeps reusing the scope without a second activation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A write to tracker B is judged by tracker B's guards whether or not a scope for tracker A is open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Inside a scope opened for tracker A, a write to tracker B runs under A's registrations and B's guards are skipped"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1656","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-21T20:18:59.522Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-21T20:18:59.522Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: pm search for 'extension scope reused for another tracker nested dispatch' returned no item about per-tracker scope identity."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e2e9d329309e212ec7bffccee4af038d22333f2805396171330d158245d0bdf3","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7766d0d76a47fb544259328795cb99cecb54bad8a40bcaac8dd7e39c94fa2cfc"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T21:42:47.395Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-2","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"df02aa70db5bf450de2ff7ae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-2","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-21T21:42:47.394Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Additional scope from the third Codex review of PR 1764: runAction with an explicit cwd holds the activation gate's write slot while its command runs, but does not mark an active scope. A command that then calls runInActiveExtensionScope, runWithActiveExtensions or a plain nested runAction for the same tracker waits for a read slot that cannot open until the command returns. The fix belongs with scope identity: a dispatch should publish the scope (and its tracker root) it already holds, so nested same-root work reuses it."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T21:42:47.395Z"}],"before_hash":"e2e9d329309e212ec7bffccee4af038d22333f2805396171330d158245d0bdf3","after_hash":"33b195f8d2cdd14abda6d4adfc8511cd6f52338bdd14c665e708d735aa7ac2cd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0fab1c2e6ef663535b44348f47ec7a6c2b27c8e1435c87abdb46850b189bb569"}
